1
00:02:04,139 --> 00:02:08,229
No animals were hurt during the
production of this video.

2
00:02:08,943 --> 00:02:12,494
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:12,494 --> 00:02:13,280
Go!

4
00:02:13,450 --> 00:02:14,900
Go! Go!

5
00:02:42,463 --> 00:02:43,973
Search around!

6
00:02:44,544 --> 00:02:46,614
He is wounded!
He can't go too far!

7
00:03:31,337 --> 00:03:33,077
I have to go.

8
00:03:36,807 --> 00:03:38,387
The mine!

9
00:03:40,809 --> 00:03:42,609
The mine!

10
00:03:46,388 --> 00:03:47,968
The mine!

11
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:50,769
The mine!

12
00:04:10,171 --> 00:04:11,611
To the mine!

13
00:04:13,494 --> 00:04:14,984
To the mine!

14
00:05:03,255 --> 00:05:04,875
People!

15
00:05:04,964 --> 00:05:07,074
Hear me out!

16
00:05:08,131 --> 00:05:11,777
Ertugrul Ghazi's son Kayi's Bey Osman Bey...

17
00:05:11,777 --> 00:05:13,727
...is a rebel guilty!

18
00:05:16,085 --> 00:05:19,865
He disobeyed Seljuq
He run away from the judge.

19
00:05:20,706 --> 00:05:23,776
He'll be punished when he is found!

20
00:05:25,529 --> 00:05:27,419
Hear me out!

21
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:35,130
Watch who you are talking about!

22
00:05:40,378 --> 00:05:42,428
Osman Bey wouldn't do such a thing!

23
00:06:34,945 --> 00:06:36,595
Vizier Alam-shah!

24
00:06:44,901 --> 00:06:48,251
What you are doing to Osman Bey
is not Turkish tradition.

25
00:06:50,785 --> 00:06:52,705
Malhun Hatun.

26
00:06:53,058 --> 00:06:55,388
Umur Bey's beloved daughter.

27
00:06:55,583 --> 00:06:58,523
The mother of Osman Bey's heir.

28
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:05,300
I am so sorry to see you under
these conditions.

29
00:07:06,059 --> 00:07:08,879
Your face says how sorry you are, really.

30
00:07:10,673 --> 00:07:12,823
Don't tire yourself.

31
00:07:14,306 --> 00:07:18,066
No, no. I really am sorry.

32
00:07:19,592 --> 00:07:23,232
Because I believe Osman Bey is innocent.

33
00:07:24,006 --> 00:07:27,106
But why would someone like Osman Bey...

34
00:07:27,476 --> 00:07:31,226
...run away from the judgment...

35
00:07:31,984 --> 00:07:34,074
...even without denying the accusations?

36
00:07:35,768 --> 00:07:39,888
Obviously, there is something he hides.

37
00:07:40,917 --> 00:07:44,717
My Bey does everything on a purpose.

38
00:07:45,239 --> 00:07:48,139
I have no doubt that he is innocent.

39
00:07:49,937 --> 00:07:53,507
Osman Bey and I experienced
many troubles.

40
00:07:53,877 --> 00:07:58,557
And we know how to get rid of them.

41
00:07:59,299 --> 00:08:01,249
Don't worry about that.

42
00:08:02,941 --> 00:08:06,191
You are going to remember these days,
Vizier Alam Shah.

43
00:08:19,293 --> 00:08:20,933
Hadrat Vizier.

44
00:08:21,384 --> 00:08:25,424
The announcers yell that Osman Bey
is a betrayer...

45
00:08:25,424 --> 00:08:26,994
...as you ordered.

46
00:08:29,137 --> 00:08:34,607
Then it is time to visit Kayi tents.

47
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,630
O The Healer!

48
00:10:33,999 --> 00:10:37,569
They couldn't take Osman Bey to Konya.
He got rid of them.

49
00:10:38,727 --> 00:10:42,237
But where is he now?
What is he doing?

50
00:10:42,401 --> 00:10:44,271
Don't worry, daughter.

51
00:10:44,863 --> 00:10:46,813
No one should worry.

52
00:10:48,007 --> 00:10:50,827
We will overcome this
with Allah's permission.

53
00:10:51,474 --> 00:10:53,484
We will for sure.

54
00:10:53,561 --> 00:10:56,666
Also, Osman wouldn't go with the men
of that Vizier...

55
00:10:56,666 --> 00:10:59,846
...if he hadn't had a plan.

56
00:11:01,519 --> 00:11:03,879
He must have a plan.

57
00:11:05,927 --> 00:11:09,867
The first thing I'll do is to...

58
00:11:10,233 --> 00:11:11,933
...go to Konya to see Sultan Mesut.

59
00:11:13,478 --> 00:11:17,758
I have to talk about what
all of this is about.

60
00:11:18,342 --> 00:11:22,679
Before we understand what's going on,
they are going to come at us as they see..

61
00:11:22,679 --> 00:11:24,829
...the empty throne of Kayi.

62
00:11:25,978 --> 00:11:29,048
However, Osman Bey will solve
this problem as well.

63
00:11:29,734 --> 00:11:32,264
Kayi's throne cannot stay empty!

64
00:11:43,203 --> 00:11:45,413
Give me patience, the messenger of Allah!

65
00:11:47,827 --> 00:11:49,757
Vizier Alam-shah is coming!

66
00:12:03,305 --> 00:12:05,815
Mari! My dear wife!

67
00:12:16,742 --> 00:12:18,962
You look better.

68
00:12:19,695 --> 00:12:24,535
The Turkish dress was awful!

69
00:12:24,821 --> 00:12:26,377
It was terrible!

70
00:12:26,377 --> 00:12:27,917
You looked like a shepherd!

71
00:12:30,054 --> 00:12:31,744
But now...

72
00:12:32,804 --> 00:12:34,254
...look at you!

73
00:12:35,623 --> 00:12:37,993
You are like a real princess.

74
00:12:41,652 --> 00:12:46,242
What makes a human powerful and honorable
is not their dress, Nicola.

75
00:12:47,619 --> 00:12:50,219
That Osman and Turgut and all
who you cannot defeat...

76
00:12:50,484 --> 00:12:54,294
...their source for power is here.

77
00:12:56,933 --> 00:12:58,733
But you don't have that.

78
00:12:59,924 --> 00:13:02,424
You will never be the man I want.

79
00:13:11,810 --> 00:13:14,010
Where are you now, Mari?

80
00:13:17,195 --> 00:13:19,245
You are in my castle.

81
00:13:21,094 --> 00:13:23,084
You are with me.

82
00:13:24,812 --> 00:13:27,442
Those men who you think powerful...

83
00:13:28,186 --> 00:13:31,916
...didn't even realise
while I was getting you!

84
00:13:32,779 --> 00:13:35,519
This is power, you get it?

85
00:13:36,227 --> 00:13:38,277
This is pure power!

86
00:13:38,611 --> 00:13:41,711
Is it enough?
No, it's not!

87
00:13:41,923 --> 00:13:45,893
More power!
More! More!

88
00:13:47,807 --> 00:13:49,397
Where is Kornelia?

89
00:13:50,264 --> 00:13:52,364
I asked around, no one saw her.

90
00:13:52,732 --> 00:13:55,262
She is resting.

91
00:13:56,292 --> 00:13:58,582
My dear wife Mari.

92
00:14:00,301 --> 00:14:02,781
This is our first dinner.

93
00:14:04,812 --> 00:14:10,012
I have a very special
meal prepared for you.

94
00:14:11,942 --> 00:14:14,532
The most special meal I'll eat...

95
00:14:15,858 --> 00:14:18,938
...is the meal I'll eat with you
for the last time, Nicola.

96
00:14:42,855 --> 00:14:45,605
What was your friend's name?

97
00:14:47,351 --> 00:14:50,161
Kornia... no no!
Kornelia!

98
00:14:55,164 --> 00:14:58,344
Well-cooked Kornelia.

99
00:15:31,553 --> 00:15:34,203
The barrels are burning!
There is a fire!

100
00:15:34,559 --> 00:15:36,497
Run!

101
00:15:36,497 --> 00:15:38,087
Fire!

102
00:15:38,568 --> 00:15:41,598
Bring water!
Run!

103
00:16:38,423 --> 00:16:40,449
It's Turkish tradition.

104
00:16:40,449 --> 00:16:44,559
The throne, the position of Bey
cannot be empty.

105
00:16:47,535 --> 00:16:48,905
The owner of the throne...

106
00:16:50,165 --> 00:16:54,415
...the Bey of the tribe is still alive.

107
00:16:54,693 --> 00:16:56,183
Thank Allah.

108
00:16:58,626 --> 00:17:00,846
When the situation changes...

109
00:17:01,239 --> 00:17:05,049
...we'll start talking about this.

110
00:17:11,381 --> 00:17:13,101
Sheik Edebali.

111
00:17:13,612 --> 00:17:16,502
You are absolutely right.

112
00:17:16,955 --> 00:17:20,205
But we are not in a peace era.

113
00:17:21,113 --> 00:17:24,045
The enemy surrounded us.

114
00:17:24,045 --> 00:17:26,805
The Lords are greedy.

115
00:17:29,548 --> 00:17:32,738
What are you trying to say, Alam shah?

116
00:17:35,142 --> 00:17:38,716
Make the long story short.

117
00:17:38,716 --> 00:17:40,906
Say what you have to say.

118
00:17:42,146 --> 00:17:44,476
You are right, old woman.

119
00:17:46,534 --> 00:17:50,294
Let's make the long story short.

120
00:17:53,497 --> 00:17:56,327
While Osman Bey is absent...

121
00:17:59,429 --> 00:18:02,109
Someone needs to sit on the throne.

122
00:18:04,394 --> 00:18:08,894
And that person is Gündüz Bey.

123
00:18:18,738 --> 00:18:20,958
As my Sheik said...

124
00:18:21,908 --> 00:18:24,018
...Osman Bey is alive.

125
00:18:24,309 --> 00:18:26,339
No one else is needed.

126
00:18:30,593 --> 00:18:35,033
It's not the right time to talk about this,
Vizier Alam shah.

127
00:18:35,986 --> 00:18:37,996
This is unnecessary now

128
00:18:41,092 --> 00:18:44,392
It is apparent that you misunderstood me.

129
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:48,820
I am not asking.

130
00:18:49,724 --> 00:18:51,664
I am ordering.

131
00:18:58,479 --> 00:19:01,039
Inegol Castle.

132
00:19:04,337 --> 00:19:06,677
I'll kill you!

133
00:19:07,064 --> 00:19:08,764
I'll kill you!

134
00:19:09,013 --> 00:19:11,048
I'll kill you!
How can you do this?

135
00:19:11,048 --> 00:19:15,408
What did you think, Mari, huh?
Did you think I was really in love with you?

136
00:19:16,380 --> 00:19:17,960
What did you think?

137
00:19:19,007 --> 00:19:23,537
I was going to marry you only for
political issues! Only for political issues!

138
00:19:23,856 --> 00:19:25,186
I'll kill you!

139
00:19:25,186 --> 00:19:27,636
But what did you do?

140
00:19:27,649 --> 00:19:31,155
You humiliated me.
You humiliated me!

141
00:19:31,155 --> 00:19:33,765
You dishonored me!

142
00:19:34,754 --> 00:19:38,194
I don't forget, Mari!
I don't forget, understand? I don't!

143
00:19:38,253 --> 00:19:40,513
I just wait!

144
00:19:54,849 --> 00:19:56,849
My dear wife.

145
00:19:58,597 --> 00:20:00,407
Goodbye.

146
00:20:08,254 --> 00:20:09,544
Mari.

147
00:20:10,090 --> 00:20:11,570
Mari.

148
00:20:15,863 --> 00:20:17,493
Turgut!

149
00:20:17,939 --> 00:20:19,529
It's okay.

150
00:20:21,122 --> 00:20:22,682
Hang on.

151
00:21:08,571 --> 00:21:10,111
Come on!

152
00:21:11,510 --> 00:21:14,760
Get me out of here!
Save me!

153
00:21:15,074 --> 00:21:16,934
Get me out of here!

154
00:21:17,094 --> 00:21:19,354
Please save me!

155
00:21:20,840 --> 00:21:23,170
Get me out of here!

156
00:21:24,326 --> 00:21:26,476
Kornelia!
Are you okay?

157
00:21:27,412 --> 00:21:30,302
- Thank God.
- We are here to save you.

158
00:21:30,616 --> 00:21:32,286
Where is Lord's room?

159
00:21:32,371 --> 00:21:33,829
There are many soldiers outside!

160
00:21:33,829 --> 00:21:35,799
Where is Lord's room?

161
00:21:38,624 --> 00:21:40,324
Follow me.

162
00:21:41,132 --> 00:21:42,562
Let's go.

163
00:22:02,602 --> 00:22:05,416
Your death is here Nicola!
I am your death!

164
00:22:06,756 --> 00:22:08,326
Turgut!

165
00:22:10,986 --> 00:22:12,416
Mari.

166
00:22:34,570 --> 00:22:37,180
- Mari!
- Hurry up my Bey! They're coming!

167
00:22:38,782 --> 00:22:40,152
The secret passage.

168
00:22:40,811 --> 00:22:42,941
Take this to the secret passage, Kutay.

169
00:22:43,591 --> 00:22:45,501
Come on! Come on!

170
00:22:46,828 --> 00:22:48,978
Let's go, come on!

171
00:22:52,113 --> 00:22:54,143
You'll be fine, Mari.
Let's go!

172
00:22:55,441 --> 00:22:56,961
Go go!

173
00:23:01,540 --> 00:23:03,760
Don't let them get away!

174
00:23:08,971 --> 00:23:11,281
Soldier!

175
00:23:12,381 --> 00:23:14,181
Soldier!

176
00:23:14,698 --> 00:23:16,598
Soldier!

177
00:23:18,789 --> 00:23:21,249
Hold the doors!

178
00:23:21,670 --> 00:23:24,410
Leave me!
Go hold the doors shut!

179
00:23:24,549 --> 00:23:26,179
The doors!

180
00:23:26,518 --> 00:23:29,398
Mari, wake up, Mari!

181
00:23:29,398 --> 00:23:31,505
- Kornelia!
- Mari!

182
00:23:45,846 --> 00:23:48,156
Go, go!
Where is Kutay?

183
00:24:01,260 --> 00:24:03,230
- Go!
- Go!

184
00:24:12,252 --> 00:24:14,552
Run! Run!

185
00:24:14,637 --> 00:24:17,397
Hold the doors shut!

186
00:24:17,598 --> 00:24:18,844
Leave me!

187
00:24:18,844 --> 00:24:20,964
Hold the doors shut!

188
00:24:45,968 --> 00:24:47,248
Come here.

189
00:24:52,113 --> 00:24:54,753
Mari!
She is waking up!

190
00:24:55,218 --> 00:24:57,428
She is waking up!
Mari!

191
00:24:57,650 --> 00:24:59,700
You are fine, right?
You are fine.

192
00:25:00,497 --> 00:25:02,787
- Tugrut.
- I am here.

193
00:25:02,831 --> 00:25:04,351
I am here.

194
00:25:07,810 --> 00:25:10,650
My Bey, we have no time.
They'll find us.

195
00:25:11,586 --> 00:25:13,586
Okay, we are leaving.
Hold Mari.

196
00:25:13,915 --> 00:25:15,380
Hold Mari.

197
00:25:15,380 --> 00:25:17,190
Easy, easy.

198
00:25:17,212 --> 00:25:19,752
Bring Mari.
Come on!

199
00:25:22,659 --> 00:25:26,089
Come on, easy, easy.

200
00:25:26,192 --> 00:25:28,612
Come mari, easy.

201
00:26:42,136 --> 00:26:44,026
Thank Allah.

202
00:26:52,901 --> 00:26:55,951
Gündüz Bey, my Bey trusted you!

203
00:26:56,125 --> 00:26:59,405
Now instead of looking for him, you are
taking his place!

204
00:27:00,004 --> 00:27:02,314
You are talking to your Bey, Malhun Hatun!

205
00:27:02,338 --> 00:27:04,108
Hear yourself.

206
00:27:10,280 --> 00:27:12,310
Osman became a rebel.

207
00:27:12,572 --> 00:27:14,802
You were there too.

208
00:27:15,523 --> 00:27:17,243
I obeyed.

209
00:27:18,866 --> 00:27:21,676
What would happen if I revolted too?

210
00:27:23,638 --> 00:27:27,138
-Vizier Alemşah--
-He is setting Osman up!

211
00:27:28,654 --> 00:27:31,724
Don't you see this?

212
00:27:34,269 --> 00:27:36,769
Vizier is doing his duty.

213
00:27:37,569 --> 00:27:39,839
He wants to do nothing but help.

214
00:27:41,569 --> 00:27:44,349
People are happy since he came.

215
00:27:45,770 --> 00:27:49,590
He is helping the tribes, keeping peace
with the Lords.

216
00:27:51,098 --> 00:27:55,658
Isn't this bloodshed is enough,
Malhun Hatun?

217
00:28:00,121 --> 00:28:03,631
Do you ever learn from the past, Gündüz?

218
00:28:05,363 --> 00:28:10,353
Vizier is trying to break the tribe apart.

219
00:28:11,649 --> 00:28:14,073
Look, you are there...

220
00:28:14,073 --> 00:28:15,583
...we are here.

221
00:28:16,031 --> 00:28:18,141
He already broke us.

222
00:28:20,836 --> 00:28:24,426
Do you know where and how your brother is?

223
00:28:25,287 --> 00:28:26,857
Mother...

224
00:28:28,282 --> 00:28:31,352
...Osman revolted against the Sultan.

225
00:28:31,793 --> 00:28:33,263
He is running.

226
00:28:34,068 --> 00:28:36,398
I am here for the sake of my tribe.

227
00:28:36,422 --> 00:28:38,772
What about Osman?

228
00:28:40,381 --> 00:28:43,171
You think about the tribe
but not your brother.

229
00:28:43,645 --> 00:28:45,645
Where and how Osman is?

230
00:28:47,286 --> 00:28:49,666
Did you get drunk in power?

231
00:28:54,123 --> 00:28:56,343
You are going too far, Malhun Hatun!

232
00:28:58,141 --> 00:29:00,301
Osman is my brother.

233
00:29:01,131 --> 00:29:04,311
I love him more than any of you do.

234
00:29:06,796 --> 00:29:09,316
But Konya's order is clear.

235
00:29:09,727 --> 00:29:13,347
I am trying to keep my tribe safe.

236
00:29:13,801 --> 00:29:17,061
Then, Gündüz Bey...

237
00:29:19,020 --> 00:29:22,340
...first, go after Mari who was
taken from our tribe.

238
00:29:26,564 --> 00:29:29,224
Our guest got kidnapped.

239
00:29:30,878 --> 00:29:33,948
Tell me, who did this?

240
00:29:39,945 --> 00:29:41,575
Bala is right.

241
00:29:42,575 --> 00:29:44,635
If you sit on the throne...

242
00:29:44,871 --> 00:29:47,331
...then first, find the traitor among us.

243
00:29:55,583 --> 00:29:59,602
After that, take my Osman's valiant
alps...

244
00:29:59,602 --> 00:30:01,972
...from the Vizier.

245
00:30:03,897 --> 00:30:06,127
They are Kayı's alps.

246
00:30:06,316 --> 00:30:08,246
They are innocent.

247
00:30:14,773 --> 00:30:17,003
Hatuns!

248
00:30:17,216 --> 00:30:19,446
It is time for us to leave.

249
00:30:21,855 --> 00:30:24,895
Gündğz Bey has a lot of work to do.

250
00:30:36,884 --> 00:30:38,384
Gündüz...

251
00:30:39,028 --> 00:30:40,948
...what will we do now?

252
00:30:44,869 --> 00:30:48,229
Is it the right thing to trust the Vizier?

253
00:30:48,272 --> 00:30:50,022
I did what I did...

254
00:30:51,525 --> 00:30:53,295
...for my tribe, Ayşe.

255
00:30:56,006 --> 00:30:58,506
You keep an eye on Malhun and Bala.

256
00:31:00,732 --> 00:31:02,892
They won't stay still.

257
00:31:15,620 --> 00:31:17,080
My Vizier...

258
00:31:17,315 --> 00:31:19,475
...we followed Osman for a long
while but...

259
00:31:20,273 --> 00:31:22,793
...we lost his track in the dark.

260
00:31:24,304 --> 00:31:25,864
We surrendered the woods.

261
00:31:26,422 --> 00:31:29,422
I will go back at the first light.

262
00:31:30,255 --> 00:31:32,095
He is wounded.

263
00:31:32,332 --> 00:31:34,082
He has nowhere to go.

264
00:31:34,799 --> 00:31:36,709
Good.

265
00:31:36,974 --> 00:31:38,864
I don't want any mistakes, Konur.

266
00:31:40,540 --> 00:31:43,920
Osman will be beheaded as he is seen.

267
00:31:45,094 --> 00:31:48,284
His reputation will fade with him.

268
00:31:49,045 --> 00:31:54,755
Also, anyone who helps
Osman Bey will be beheaded.

269
00:31:55,061 --> 00:31:56,891
As you order, my Vizier.

270
00:31:58,034 --> 00:31:59,594
Ferman.

271
00:32:00,051 --> 00:32:02,431
These Kayı people can do anything.

272
00:32:03,126 --> 00:32:06,256
They will try everything to get to Osman.

273
00:32:07,161 --> 00:32:09,231
Watch the tribe closely.

274
00:32:10,196 --> 00:32:14,326
I want Gündüz Bey and the Lords
at the inn.

275
00:32:17,033 --> 00:32:19,213
As you order, Vizier.

276
00:32:27,426 --> 00:32:30,186
The rebels' blood...

277
00:32:30,599 --> 00:32:33,359
...will feed the order I establish.

278
00:32:34,906 --> 00:32:36,676
In this order...

279
00:32:37,548 --> 00:32:41,498
...only those who bow to me will stand.

280
00:33:14,541 --> 00:33:16,191
My Creator.

281
00:33:38,915 --> 00:33:40,365
My Creator.

282
00:34:04,968 --> 00:34:06,498
My Creator

283
00:34:07,495 --> 00:34:08,745
My Allah, my Allah!

284
00:34:09,993 --> 00:34:12,072
Thank you.

285
00:34:27,943 --> 00:34:29,513
My Creator.

286
00:34:37,804 --> 00:34:40,224
My merciful Creator.

287
00:34:41,266 --> 00:34:44,596
My Creator, You...

288
00:34:45,438 --> 00:34:48,898
...You didn't let me stay
hungry and thirsty.

289
00:34:51,628 --> 00:34:53,878
You didn't, my Creator.

290
00:34:54,583 --> 00:34:59,263
I cannot honor my debt...

291
00:34:59,866 --> 00:35:03,446
...no matter how many times I thank you...

292
00:35:04,073 --> 00:35:07,223
...many times until I cannot speak anymore...

293
00:35:08,414 --> 00:35:10,764
...I still cannot honor my debt.

294
00:35:11,180 --> 00:35:12,810
I can't, my Creator.

295
00:35:13,580 --> 00:35:15,190
My Allah.

296
00:35:15,872 --> 00:35:21,452
How great is your mercy!
Hey Enlightened Creator!

297
00:35:23,726 --> 00:35:27,726
Praise be to Allah.
Praise be to Allah.

298
00:35:51,178 --> 00:35:53,318
I'll take revenge for you, Gonca.

299
00:35:57,237 --> 00:35:59,657
But I have to find my Bey first.

300
00:36:01,138 --> 00:36:03,358
I have to find my Bey.

301
00:36:08,325 --> 00:36:10,095
Boran.

302
00:36:11,542 --> 00:36:13,392
Don't leave, Boran.

303
00:36:15,359 --> 00:36:19,409
Even if I am angry with him,
I still need to find my Bey, Gonca.

304
00:36:20,409 --> 00:36:22,339
Don't leave.

305
00:36:23,663 --> 00:36:25,813
Don't leave, Boran.

306
00:36:30,833 --> 00:36:32,663
I won't, Gonca.

307
00:36:33,526 --> 00:36:35,426
I am not leaving anywhere.

308
00:37:33,608 --> 00:37:36,918
Soldiers! Go!

309
00:38:40,983 --> 00:38:43,243
He is in this direction
according to the tracks.

310
00:38:43,363 --> 00:38:45,233
Soldiers, go!

311
00:39:20,680 --> 00:39:22,370
You are cornered, Osman Bey!

312
00:40:18,141 --> 00:40:19,941
I found you Osman.

313
00:40:26,663 --> 00:40:28,583
Where can you run?

314
00:43:08,105 --> 00:43:10,185
Hold it, hold it!

315
00:43:10,644 --> 00:43:12,204
Take it.

316
00:44:11,261 --> 00:44:13,171
Soldiers! This way!

317
00:44:33,095 --> 00:44:35,855
He is wounded!
He cannot go too far.

318
00:44:42,787 --> 00:44:44,847
I know it is not the right time.

319
00:44:45,166 --> 00:44:48,046
But tell me.
Who abducted you?

320
00:44:48,454 --> 00:44:50,164
I don't know.

321
00:44:50,379 --> 00:44:51,959
I was fainted.

322
00:44:53,078 --> 00:44:55,458
I was in a chest when I woke up.

323
00:44:56,810 --> 00:44:59,950
Didn't you see anyone?
Do you remember anyone?

324
00:45:02,056 --> 00:45:04,356
Seljuk Soldiers...

325
00:45:04,877 --> 00:45:07,257
...they're the ones who turned me over.

326
00:45:08,846 --> 00:45:10,476
Alemshah,...

327
00:45:11,106 --> 00:45:12,610
...snake!...

328
00:45:12,610 --> 00:45:14,340
...Snake!.

329
00:45:14,751 --> 00:45:17,151
I will make you pay for this!

330
00:45:19,055 --> 00:45:20,425
And a sherbet...

331
00:45:21,944 --> 00:45:25,624
...Ayse Hatun brought me sherbet
and gave me to drink it...

332
00:45:25,971 --> 00:45:28,101
...I don't remember the rest.

333
00:45:28,764 --> 00:45:30,284
Then, Gündüz...

334
00:45:31,980 --> 00:45:34,300
...Gündüz Bey is in cahoots
with the Vizier.

335
00:45:37,080 --> 00:45:38,410
Why?

336
00:45:38,733 --> 00:45:40,853
What's the reason Gündüz?

337
00:45:41,360 --> 00:45:43,010
Why?

338
00:45:48,066 --> 00:45:51,426
Nobody is around my Bey,
they lost our track...

339
00:45:51,701 --> 00:45:54,181
- ...we can go now.
- Let's go then, Kutan.

340
00:45:54,652 --> 00:45:57,792
Let's go so that Osman Bey can
know about the traitor in his tribe.

341
00:45:59,418 --> 00:46:02,628
I'm going to go to the Kayı
tents. You be careful.

342
00:46:03,098 --> 00:46:06,018
You never know what that
weasel Nikola will do.

343
00:46:06,919 --> 00:46:08,719
Yes, my Bey.

344
00:46:08,886 --> 00:46:10,916
Alps! Let's go!

345
00:46:12,169 --> 00:46:14,099
- Let's go!
- I'm here.

346
00:46:14,111 --> 00:46:15,381
I'm here.

347
00:46:16,781 --> 00:46:18,271
I'm with you.

348
00:46:19,115 --> 00:46:20,815
I won't leave you.

349
00:46:23,776 --> 00:46:25,276
Alright, you may go.

350
00:46:29,835 --> 00:46:32,065
Ergus, is there a trace?

351
00:46:32,307 --> 00:46:34,107
There is no trace sir.

352
00:46:36,852 --> 00:46:40,612
We just got the word, that Vizier
Alemshah is waiting for you.

353
00:46:40,912 --> 00:46:44,674
That's just what we need at this moment.

354
00:46:44,674 --> 00:46:45,974
Look at the state I am.

355
00:46:47,662 --> 00:46:50,022
Kosses is probably there too.

356
00:46:51,211 --> 00:46:53,771
Kosses should never know of this Ergus!

357
00:46:53,841 --> 00:46:55,211
Never!

358
00:46:55,410 --> 00:46:59,280
I don't have time and patience for this!

359
00:47:00,390 --> 00:47:04,194
Sir, what if Kosses already knows?

360
00:47:04,194 --> 00:47:06,054
We'd know of it if that
was the case.

361
00:47:06,538 --> 00:47:08,328
I will act accordingly.

362
00:47:10,961 --> 00:47:13,147
It's not Kosses that matters...

363
00:47:13,147 --> 00:47:14,647
...he is easy,...

364
00:47:15,041 --> 00:47:16,951
...Vizier Alemshah.

365
00:47:17,240 --> 00:47:19,520
Let's see what Vizier
Alemshah's problem is.

366
00:47:20,531 --> 00:47:22,041
Let's go!

367
00:47:24,392 --> 00:47:26,292
They came with a bunch of soldiers.

368
00:47:27,472 --> 00:47:30,602
They said that coal, now
belongs to Seljuk.

369
00:47:31,474 --> 00:47:33,444
It's Vizier's order.

370
00:47:33,951 --> 00:47:36,881
He'll gather the Turkmen Beys
at the willow.

371
00:47:37,640 --> 00:47:40,120
I'd like you to come with me.

372
00:47:41,213 --> 00:47:43,053
We'll talk about this as well.

373
00:47:44,311 --> 00:47:47,041
Vizier caused a lot of trouble
to Osman Bey.

374
00:47:47,834 --> 00:47:49,904
I don't trust the Vizier, Gündüz Bey.

375
00:47:50,016 --> 00:47:54,326
Davut Agha, for now Vizier's
intent is sincere.

376
00:47:55,162 --> 00:47:57,392
You should listen to him yourself.

377
00:47:59,219 --> 00:48:01,759
Alright, I'll come.

378
00:48:01,985 --> 00:48:04,055
Let's see what he wants.

379
00:48:18,168 --> 00:48:19,708
How dare you come to our tribe!

380
00:48:55,203 --> 00:48:57,243
Message from Sultan Mesud.

381
00:48:59,541 --> 00:49:05,991
Son of Ertuğrul Ghazi Osman Bey has
disobeyed the orders of Sultan Mesud...

382
00:49:05,992 --> 00:49:07,152
...and became a rebel.

383
00:49:07,473 --> 00:49:12,353
That is why when Osman Bey is caught,
instead of bringing him on horseback...

384
00:49:13,057 --> 00:49:16,347
...he'll be dragged from the rear of the
horse all the way to Konya.

385
00:49:21,990 --> 00:49:23,420
Also...

386
00:49:24,225 --> 00:49:27,925
...if anyone tries to help Osman Bey...

387
00:49:28,323 --> 00:49:30,083
- ...their heads will be...
- Enough!

388
00:49:37,091 --> 00:49:38,741
This is Kaya Tribe!

389
00:49:41,600 --> 00:49:45,190
We are humble servants of the state...

390
00:49:47,148 --> 00:49:49,678
...you did not have to come all this way.

391
00:49:54,010 --> 00:49:59,780
If I find Osman Bey, I'll take
him to Sultan myself.

392
00:50:20,058 --> 00:50:22,382
We made the right call coming
here Gündüz Bey...

393
00:50:22,382 --> 00:50:25,302
...wanted the give you the news ourselves.

394
00:50:27,130 --> 00:50:28,720
Godspeed!

395
00:50:36,195 --> 00:50:38,495
They couldn't find Osman, mother.

396
00:50:39,428 --> 00:50:41,144
Thank Allah, my girl...

397
00:50:41,144 --> 00:50:42,924
...thank Allah!

398
00:50:55,612 --> 00:50:57,653
Everyone get back to work!

399
00:50:57,653 --> 00:50:59,663
There is nothing to see here.

400
00:51:00,426 --> 00:51:01,856
Move on!

401
00:51:11,602 --> 00:51:14,782
If you see Osman or know where he is...

402
00:51:18,332 --> 00:51:20,162
...tell me about it.

403
00:51:23,721 --> 00:51:26,021
I'll save my brother.

404
00:51:28,353 --> 00:51:30,843
Come to Gündüz Bey if that
is the case.

405
00:51:36,162 --> 00:51:38,502
Don't worry about it Gündüz Bey.

406
00:51:39,952 --> 00:51:43,802
Osman Bey will know who to contact to.

407
00:51:45,763 --> 00:51:47,433
Don't worry about it.

408
00:52:02,183 --> 00:52:03,743
Mahun Hatun,...

409
00:52:05,762 --> 00:52:07,482
...Boran Alp...

410
00:52:07,765 --> 00:52:12,405
...you won't take him with you?

411
00:52:12,993 --> 00:52:15,253
Boran is not on the
right frame of mind.

412
00:52:15,369 --> 00:52:17,839
He doesn't even know where
to stop. Don't you see?

413
00:52:30,913 --> 00:52:32,413
Ayşe,...

414
00:52:33,998 --> 00:52:36,198
...we don't know what Hatuns will do.

415
00:52:36,964 --> 00:52:39,244
If they leave the tribe, tell me about it.

416
00:52:40,502 --> 00:52:42,332
Of course, my Bey.

417
00:52:46,318 --> 00:52:48,468
Aygül, it's time to go.

418
00:52:49,089 --> 00:52:51,109
Tribe and Orhan is in your hands.

419
00:52:51,346 --> 00:52:53,956
Mother, give me your blessing.

420
00:52:54,647 --> 00:52:56,457
You may have my blessing my girl...

421
00:52:56,457 --> 00:52:58,368
...If Allah permits, come back safe.

422
00:52:59,353 --> 00:53:01,153
May Allah keep you safe.

423
00:53:01,253 --> 00:53:02,822
Don't keep us unaware.

424
00:53:02,822 --> 00:53:07,682
Thank you, Bala.

425
00:53:28,638 --> 00:53:30,468
These are Vizier Alemshah's men.

426
00:53:31,014 --> 00:53:32,924
What are they doing at the tribe?

427
00:53:38,177 --> 00:53:40,817
We'll enter from somewhere else Mari,
come on.

428
00:54:17,283 --> 00:54:18,983
Ayşe Hatun,

429
00:54:19,189 --> 00:54:20,869
I was looking for you...

430
00:54:20,994 --> 00:54:23,869
Mother, I got some business to attend
to, let's talk later.

431
00:54:23,869 --> 00:54:25,949
I know how good your engravings are...

432
00:54:25,949 --> 00:54:30,237
...mine aren't as pretty as yours.

433
00:54:31,087 --> 00:54:33,137
Can you show me how to do it?

434
00:54:35,272 --> 00:54:37,982
Okay, I'll show you.

435
00:54:42,597 --> 00:54:44,927
What are you up to Ayşe Hatun?

436
00:55:03,791 --> 00:55:05,151
Come on!

437
00:55:08,756 --> 00:55:10,976
Come on.

438
00:55:18,025 --> 00:55:21,725
Mari, Turgut Bey, hope you're both okay.

439
00:55:24,455 --> 00:55:26,815
- Malhun Hatun
- Mari?

440
00:55:27,358 --> 00:55:28,978
You're wounded!

441
00:55:29,322 --> 00:55:31,252
Slowly, slowly!

442
00:55:34,771 --> 00:55:36,751
If Allah permits, she'll be alright.

443
00:55:36,842 --> 00:55:39,052
I saw Vizier's men at the tribe.

444
00:55:39,739 --> 00:55:41,799
- Is everything okay?
- Unfortunately, no.

445
00:55:42,229 --> 00:55:44,576
Vizier tricked Osman Bey...

446
00:55:44,576 --> 00:55:46,351
...Osman Bey is now a fugitive...

447
00:55:46,351 --> 00:55:48,031
...we are looking for him.

448
00:55:48,405 --> 00:55:50,315
We can't go to the tribe then.

449
00:55:51,435 --> 00:55:53,257
You can make it Mari.

450
00:55:53,257 --> 00:55:54,707
I'll make it.

451
00:55:54,813 --> 00:55:56,563
We are coming too.

452
00:55:57,375 --> 00:55:59,945
Do you know where Osman Bey is?

453
00:56:00,738 --> 00:56:02,835
No, we don't.

454
00:56:02,835 --> 00:56:04,495
We'll look everywhere.

455
00:56:05,016 --> 00:56:07,626
Kumral Abdal will help us.

456
00:56:09,410 --> 00:56:11,550
Alright then, let's go.

457
00:56:11,554 --> 00:56:13,024
Let's go.

458
00:56:20,081 --> 00:56:22,511
It looks like they'll go to Osman Bey.

459
00:56:24,945 --> 00:56:25,865
Come on.

460
00:56:27,649 --> 00:56:30,229
We'll follow them like a shadow.

461
00:57:01,919 --> 00:57:03,669
We're coming close.

462
00:57:06,349 --> 00:57:08,259
This way!

463
00:58:00,698 --> 00:58:02,608
What are you running from?

464
00:58:03,228 --> 00:58:04,558
Who are you?

465
00:58:05,664 --> 00:58:07,204
Osman.

466
00:58:13,221 --> 00:58:15,071
Dark Osman?

467
00:58:16,206 --> 00:58:17,856
Bey Osman?

468
00:58:24,891 --> 00:58:26,531
Someone's coming!

469
00:58:30,452 --> 00:58:32,442
Are they after you or me?

470
00:58:33,064 --> 00:58:35,314
Why would they be after a shepherd?

471
00:58:36,949 --> 00:58:38,999
It looks like they're after you.

472
00:58:41,101 --> 00:58:42,871
Osman Bey,...

473
00:58:44,580 --> 00:58:46,250
...hide.

474
00:59:09,793 --> 00:59:11,453
I found you, Osman Bey.

475
00:59:45,459 --> 00:59:47,329
Did a wounded man pass here?

476
00:59:55,464 --> 00:59:57,734
I said, did a wounded man pass here?

477
01:00:03,680 --> 01:00:05,320
I'd be lying if I said anything.

478
01:00:07,706 --> 01:00:09,476
Maybe he passed...

479
01:00:09,624 --> 01:00:11,114
...but I didn't see him.

480
01:00:11,664 --> 01:00:14,994
Maybe he didn't pass but I thought he did.

481
01:00:17,525 --> 01:00:19,415
I do not know.

482
01:00:19,789 --> 01:00:22,209
Don't play word games shepherd!

483
01:00:22,320 --> 01:00:24,060
Did you see him or not?

484
01:00:24,515 --> 01:00:29,335
Maybe what I saw was more than a man...

485
01:00:30,738 --> 01:00:35,148
...maybe he has no manhood inside him.

486
01:00:38,307 --> 01:00:40,777
You're asking the question
wrong soldier agha.

487
01:00:44,345 --> 01:00:47,035
- What is your name?
- Why do you want to know my name?

488
01:00:47,386 --> 01:00:49,076
I'm just a shepherd...

489
01:00:49,076 --> 01:00:50,636
...they call me shepherd.

490
01:00:51,875 --> 01:00:53,635
Listen up, shepherd!

491
01:00:53,775 --> 01:00:57,995
If you lie to me, I'll butcher you
with my sword!

492
01:01:11,358 --> 01:01:13,438
Let's go!

493
01:01:20,723 --> 01:01:22,283
Stop!

494
01:01:59,832 --> 01:02:04,192
It was old, used to slow the herd.

495
01:02:04,925 --> 01:02:07,715
I was right about to skin it.

496
01:02:13,105 --> 01:02:15,085
Soldiers, let's move!

497
01:02:34,569 --> 01:02:36,099
Don't give up.

498
01:02:36,238 --> 01:02:38,748
Osman Bey

499
01:02:39,570 --> 01:02:40,970
Osman Bey

500
01:02:44,487 --> 01:02:46,507
Osman Bey

501
01:02:48,436 --> 01:02:50,076
Be careful.

502
01:02:50,318 --> 01:02:52,058
Let me help.

503
01:03:00,084 --> 01:03:02,544
You did a great thing.

504
01:03:03,855 --> 01:03:06,165
- Thank you.
- Thank you too.

505
01:03:07,140 --> 01:03:09,000
Come with me my Bey.

506
01:03:10,099 --> 01:03:13,039
Hang on my Bey!

507
01:03:17,566 --> 01:03:19,386
Hang on!

508
01:03:22,967 --> 01:03:24,627
Hang on my Bey!

509
01:03:28,102 --> 01:03:29,822
Careful my Bey.

510
01:03:39,455 --> 01:03:41,115
There it is.

511
01:03:43,904 --> 01:03:45,704
This is my ration my Bey.

512
01:03:46,551 --> 01:03:48,551
No, no

513
01:03:48,630 --> 01:03:50,370
- It is yours.
- My bey,

514
01:03:50,921 --> 01:03:52,787
It is yours brother

515
01:03:52,787 --> 01:03:55,667
If you take half it'll multiply.

516
01:04:05,569 --> 01:04:07,599
I will not forget your help.

517
01:04:09,610 --> 01:04:12,890
Humans are flawed...

518
01:04:13,345 --> 01:04:15,295
...people forget my bey...

519
01:04:17,829 --> 01:04:20,519
Allah is the greatest!

520
01:04:22,937 --> 01:04:27,167
I live for the people and do everything
for the people my Bey.

521
01:04:28,160 --> 01:04:30,560
How do you know I am a man
of the people?

522
01:04:31,715 --> 01:04:33,575
Maybe I'm one of the tyrants.

523
01:04:34,359 --> 01:04:36,589
What if they were looking for
me for a crime?

524
01:04:36,959 --> 01:04:38,839
How do you know?

525
01:04:39,967 --> 01:04:43,857
Even if I don't know, these
animals know my Bey.

526
01:04:44,277 --> 01:04:46,147
They can smell it.

527
01:04:47,796 --> 01:04:50,356
They could have drawn attention
on you but...

528
01:04:51,800 --> 01:04:53,580
...they shushed my Bey.

529
01:04:54,174 --> 01:04:56,494
They did not make a noise.

530
01:04:56,770 --> 01:04:59,000
They sheltered you.

531
01:04:59,462 --> 01:05:01,602
They protected you.

532
01:05:04,835 --> 01:05:07,495
I've heard a lot about you.

533
01:05:08,657 --> 01:05:10,547
Thank you, brother.

534
01:05:10,754 --> 01:05:12,474
Thank you too, my bey.

535
01:05:14,120 --> 01:05:17,170
Wherever you go they'll find you.

536
01:05:17,946 --> 01:05:20,836
But no one would think looking
at a shepherd's barracks.

537
01:05:22,983 --> 01:05:24,283
At Koryan's...

538
01:05:25,457 --> 01:05:27,547
...mountainside, I have a place...

539
01:05:28,126 --> 01:05:29,926
...go there my bey.

540
01:05:37,660 --> 01:05:39,580
Thank you.

541
01:05:40,351 --> 01:05:42,791
If I overcome this trouble...

542
01:05:44,108 --> 01:05:47,688
You will my bey, you will.

543
01:05:48,359 --> 01:05:51,609
High mountains will have denser mist.

544
01:05:53,073 --> 01:05:54,733
I'll...

545
01:05:55,545 --> 01:05:57,795
I'll never forget you.

546
01:06:16,107 --> 01:06:18,227
Praise be!

547
01:06:19,363 --> 01:06:21,443
Praise be!

548
01:06:58,760 --> 01:07:00,700
Come at me!

549
01:07:43,565 --> 01:07:45,355
Brother,...

550
01:07:51,578 --> 01:07:53,578
What are you doing here?

551
01:07:55,380 --> 01:07:57,810
I'm looking for Osman Bey.

552
01:08:00,915 --> 01:08:02,655
Who is this Osman Bey?

553
01:08:03,904 --> 01:08:06,037
Why are you looking for him?

554
01:08:06,037 --> 01:08:08,057
He fights the infidels...

555
01:08:10,725 --> 01:08:12,805
...protects the weak.

556
01:08:13,483 --> 01:08:16,372
Why would I not look for
a bey like that agha?

557
01:08:19,448 --> 01:08:21,309
Then,...

558
01:08:23,058 --> 01:08:25,438
...he is right in front of you.

559
01:08:30,738 --> 01:08:32,548
No,...

560
01:08:33,060 --> 01:08:34,950
...no need for that brother.

561
01:08:36,227 --> 01:08:37,716
No need for that.

562
01:08:37,897 --> 01:08:39,287
The bow that is stretched,...

563
01:08:39,948 --> 01:08:41,678
...the arrow that's stuck,...

564
01:08:41,880 --> 01:08:44,399
...stolen equipment....

565
01:08:44,638 --> 01:08:46,417
...is at your command Osman Bey.

566
01:08:48,304 --> 01:08:50,084
State your name.

567
01:08:50,274 --> 01:08:51,886
It's Durahan, my bey.

568
01:08:51,886 --> 01:08:53,746
I am at your command.

569
01:08:57,136 --> 01:08:59,127
You are not from here
that much is clear.

570
01:08:59,479 --> 01:09:01,099
Where do you come from?

571
01:09:01,147 --> 01:09:03,117
I come from Caucasia my bey.

572
01:09:03,937 --> 01:09:06,057
Praise be!

573
01:09:06,796 --> 01:09:11,076
Caucasia is famous for its eagles
and valiants.

574
01:09:12,799 --> 01:09:14,249
Thank you!

575
01:09:14,312 --> 01:09:16,011
Welcome!

576
01:09:16,661 --> 01:09:18,001
Thank you.

577
01:09:18,252 --> 01:09:19,983
You're with me now.

578
01:09:21,805 --> 01:09:23,377
Let's go.

579
01:09:23,377 --> 01:09:25,118
Come on.

580
01:09:44,225 --> 01:09:46,426
Did anyone pass here shepherd?

581
01:09:58,614 --> 01:10:00,124
Let's go!

582
01:10:25,663 --> 01:10:29,483
Is Osman Bey a traitor?
Why punish his helpers?

583
01:10:30,383 --> 01:10:32,983
Is this fair, Alemshah?

584
01:10:33,104 --> 01:10:34,914
It is fair Gündüz Bey.

585
01:10:35,503 --> 01:10:39,923
He has accepted all the convictions
given to him by escaping.

586
01:10:42,595 --> 01:10:47,675
Isn't disobeying Sultan's orders treason?

587
01:10:50,484 --> 01:10:53,534
You are the son of Ertuğrul Ghazi.

588
01:10:55,256 --> 01:10:59,746
Is your loyalty to Osman or your tribe?

589
01:11:02,981 --> 01:11:04,451
My tribe.

590
01:11:05,747 --> 01:11:07,837
I thought so too.

591
01:11:09,343 --> 01:11:11,733
Keep an eye on your people.

592
01:11:11,996 --> 01:11:15,106
We would not want anyone to get hurt.

593
01:11:16,115 --> 01:11:20,415
Alps are Kayi alps.

594
01:11:20,551 --> 01:11:22,747
When will you release them?

595
01:11:22,747 --> 01:11:25,707
No Kayi alp is taken hostage.

596
01:11:27,465 --> 01:11:30,695
The ones that are kept are Osman's alps.

597
01:11:31,685 --> 01:11:33,605
Not Kayi alps.

598
01:11:36,034 --> 01:11:40,964
If I release them they'll go after Osman
and burn themselves along with you.

599
01:11:42,644 --> 01:11:47,434
I'll send them to Konya. They will
be at Sultan Mesut's hands.

600
01:11:49,119 --> 01:11:51,879
If they don't do anything crazy
on their way over there...

601
01:11:52,071 --> 01:11:54,431
...they will be spared Gündüz Bey.

602
01:12:01,230 --> 01:12:04,400
We got more important things to talk about

603
01:12:06,587 --> 01:12:09,087
It has to do with tribes future.

604
01:12:16,365 --> 01:12:19,135
Vizier your excellence, The Lords are here.

605
01:13:07,080 --> 01:13:09,450
How is Mari, Nikola?

606
01:13:09,750 --> 01:13:11,650
Is she still angry?

607
01:13:11,919 --> 01:13:14,149
Mari is my precious stone Kosses.

608
01:13:14,193 --> 01:13:17,143
I'm doing everything I can to make
her feel good but...

609
01:13:17,808 --> 01:13:20,558
...she is a bit, you know...

610
01:13:20,859 --> 01:13:22,819
...- combative.
- Nikola,...

611
01:13:23,699 --> 01:13:26,749
...she is angry at me.

612
01:13:27,249 --> 01:13:31,449
Whatever mistake she may make,
she is my most precious.

613
01:13:31,866 --> 01:13:35,186
She is a clever girl. She'll
understand us overtime.

614
01:13:37,802 --> 01:13:41,232
I think we should give it some time.

615
01:13:43,276 --> 01:13:46,986
Look, as I was returning from
Constantinople...

616
01:13:46,986 --> 01:13:50,476
...Osman has become a traitor for Seljuk.

617
01:13:51,316 --> 01:13:53,146
Vizier is on our side...

618
01:13:53,146 --> 01:13:54,877
...and we're at the willow.

619
01:13:54,877 --> 01:13:57,767
That's true. You are
correct, my saint friend.

620
01:14:02,331 --> 01:14:04,561
Does it smell like victory?

621
01:14:16,356 --> 01:14:20,906
Who would know I would be
right by Osman Bey, right bey?

622
01:14:52,487 --> 01:14:54,216
Durahan stop!

623
01:14:54,216 --> 01:14:55,966
Stop.

624
01:14:56,081 --> 01:14:58,265
- Osman Bey!
- Turgut Bey.

625
01:14:58,265 --> 01:14:59,785
Osman Bey.

626
01:14:59,955 --> 01:15:01,835
- Are you okay?
- I'm okay.

627
01:15:02,335 --> 01:15:04,240
I am fine. Don't worry.

628
01:15:04,843 --> 01:15:07,383
Thankfully, thankfully, Osman Bey.

629
01:15:08,525 --> 01:15:11,055
Come here.

630
01:15:11,530 --> 01:15:13,120
Come here.

631
01:15:15,261 --> 01:15:16,761
My Osman!

632
01:15:17,375 --> 01:15:18,845
Malhun!

633
01:15:19,494 --> 01:15:21,094
Osman!

634
01:15:22,942 --> 01:15:24,702
My Bey!

635
01:15:26,996 --> 01:15:28,671
You are wounded.

636
01:15:28,671 --> 01:15:31,271
Don't worry, I am fine.

637
01:15:32,732 --> 01:15:35,222
- You are?
- I am. Don't worry.

638
01:15:35,305 --> 01:15:37,015
How did you find me?

639
01:15:40,849 --> 01:15:42,429
Good luck, brother.

640
01:15:44,471 --> 01:15:48,091
No luck comes when you say it.

641
01:15:48,660 --> 01:15:51,330
We are looking for a Bey.

642
01:15:51,380 --> 01:15:53,470
Have you seen one, Çoban Agha?

643
01:15:53,809 --> 01:15:57,279
If found by looking, everyone would find.

644
01:15:57,833 --> 01:15:59,833
Why are you looking for him?

645
01:16:00,690 --> 01:16:04,290
It doesn't matter why. Have you seen him
or not. It is urgent!

646
01:16:06,180 --> 01:16:09,610
Malhun Hatun, let's not confuse him.

647
01:16:12,085 --> 01:16:15,085
He won't talk that way.

648
01:16:15,726 --> 01:16:17,016
Confuse.

649
01:16:17,597 --> 01:16:20,837
I won't get confused.

650
01:16:26,508 --> 01:16:28,348
Osman Bey.

651
01:16:31,194 --> 01:16:33,194
Don't worry, brother.

652
01:16:33,502 --> 01:16:35,962
We are his friends, that's why.

653
01:16:38,694 --> 01:16:40,294
Now, tell us...

654
01:16:40,544 --> 01:16:42,174
...where he went.

655
01:16:46,934 --> 01:16:49,084
They are his friends.

656
01:16:54,016 --> 01:16:55,726
This way.

657
01:16:56,346 --> 01:16:58,230
He went to the Harmanlık way.

658
01:16:58,230 --> 01:17:01,460
-But he was walking, hurry up.
-Thank you!

659
01:17:06,111 --> 01:17:08,241
May Allah bless that shepherd.

660
01:17:10,581 --> 01:17:12,571
Sit, let me take a look at your wound.

661
01:17:13,863 --> 01:17:15,873
-Come here.
-Sit.

662
01:17:22,654 --> 01:17:24,634
In the name of Allah!

663
01:17:35,507 --> 01:17:37,357
Allah is the healer.

664
01:17:47,125 --> 01:17:48,725
Thank you.

665
01:17:49,173 --> 01:17:50,713
Thank you.

666
01:17:54,525 --> 01:17:57,495
My Bey, we came prepared.

667
01:18:09,198 --> 01:18:10,848
Osman Bey.

668
01:18:15,191 --> 01:18:16,731
Turahan Alp.

669
01:18:18,732 --> 01:18:20,972
Choose our road...

670
01:18:21,669 --> 01:18:23,969
...and came after us.

671
01:18:27,084 --> 01:18:29,024
From now on, he is my alp.

672
01:18:29,496 --> 01:18:31,026
Also...

673
01:18:31,311 --> 01:18:33,551
...I owe him my life.

674
01:18:35,042 --> 01:18:38,102
My life is yours on this way, my Bey.

675
01:18:38,286 --> 01:18:40,616
-May you be with us.
-Thank you.

676
01:18:42,060 --> 01:18:43,630
Thank you.

677
01:18:45,800 --> 01:18:47,360
Come on, eat.

678
01:18:47,768 --> 01:18:49,578
Friends.

679
01:18:55,034 --> 01:18:56,964
Mari?

680
01:18:58,270 --> 01:18:59,970
Are you well?

681
01:19:00,844 --> 01:19:02,564
She is, now.

682
01:19:03,822 --> 01:19:05,966
But that dog Nikola...

683
01:19:06,266 --> 01:19:08,876
...wounded Mari, in front of my eyes.

684
01:19:10,644 --> 01:19:12,514
But I am fine now.

685
01:19:14,069 --> 01:19:16,129
How did that dog...

686
01:19:16,782 --> 01:19:18,432
...kidnap you?

687
01:19:19,034 --> 01:19:22,174
Tell me. We will not let anyone
get to you!

688
01:19:22,539 --> 01:19:25,029
The last thing I remember is...

689
01:19:25,159 --> 01:19:27,519
...the sherbet Ayşe Hatun brought.

690
01:19:27,696 --> 01:19:29,126
I drank it.

691
01:19:30,126 --> 01:19:33,756
When I woke up I was with the Vizier
Alemşah's men.

692
01:19:35,538 --> 01:19:37,668
Then, Turgut came.

693
01:19:43,328 --> 01:19:46,598
My Bey, Söğüt is confused.

694
01:19:47,485 --> 01:19:51,055
Sultan Mesut told everyone he will behead
everyone who helps you.

695
01:19:52,248 --> 01:19:54,618
That snake Vizier.

696
01:19:56,323 --> 01:19:58,193
He poisoned Sultan too.

697
01:19:58,940 --> 01:20:01,030
His aim was to make me alone.

698
01:20:02,564 --> 01:20:04,094
But...

699
01:20:05,896 --> 01:20:08,106
...there is something else.

700
01:20:10,708 --> 01:20:13,318
Bala? Orhan?

701
01:20:14,399 --> 01:20:16,419
How is the tribe?
Tell me!

702
01:20:18,746 --> 01:20:21,256
How are they?

703
01:20:24,887 --> 01:20:26,477
Gündüz Bey.

704
01:20:30,231 --> 01:20:33,721
Vizier sat Gündüz Bey to your place,
my Bey.

705
01:20:39,497 --> 01:20:42,657
Gündüz Bey is with the Vizier.

706
01:20:47,520 --> 01:20:49,290
What are you saying?

707
01:20:54,381 --> 01:20:56,931
My brother is with the Vizier.

708
01:21:15,758 --> 01:21:18,188
Vizier Alemşah!

709
01:21:38,090 --> 01:21:41,420
The Kayı Tribe's real bey...

710
01:21:41,494 --> 01:21:43,334
...Gündüz Bey!

711
01:22:01,759 --> 01:22:03,879
Here you go.

712
01:22:14,134 --> 01:22:16,484
How many soldiers did you lose, Nikola?

713
01:22:18,097 --> 01:22:20,507
Hundreds? Thousands?

714
01:22:22,072 --> 01:22:24,412
What about you, Lords?

715
01:22:25,094 --> 01:22:26,764
Rogatus?

716
01:22:27,180 --> 01:22:29,270
Kosses?

717
01:22:30,700 --> 01:22:34,790
What about you, you great Beys?

718
01:22:36,045 --> 01:22:38,795
How many alps did you bury?

719
01:22:39,655 --> 01:22:41,695
How many martyrs?

720
01:22:44,657 --> 01:22:48,487
Si vis pacem, para bellum.

721
01:22:53,971 --> 01:22:57,541
If you want peace, get ready for a war.

722
01:23:01,280 --> 01:23:04,170
Forget about these lines, Lords.

723
01:23:05,016 --> 01:23:08,106
I promise you peace without a war.

724
01:23:11,106 --> 01:23:14,666
Now it is time to stop the bloodshed.

725
01:23:16,383 --> 01:23:18,773
So, Vizier Alemşah.

726
01:23:19,218 --> 01:23:21,188
How do you plan on doing that?

727
01:23:23,044 --> 01:23:28,014
Since there is always a war on
these lands.

728
01:23:29,665 --> 01:23:32,505
What is the situation of your subjects,
Nikola?

729
01:23:35,017 --> 01:23:37,227
What about yours'?

730
01:23:39,943 --> 01:23:41,833
What about you?

731
01:23:42,543 --> 01:23:45,213
Is there abundance in your tribes?

732
01:23:50,810 --> 01:23:52,790
There will be abundence.

733
01:23:52,900 --> 01:23:54,870
There will be happiness.

734
01:23:55,089 --> 01:23:58,509
This will provide peace.

735
01:24:02,353 --> 01:24:04,853
Prosperity takes effort.

736
01:24:08,647 --> 01:24:10,917
What is your plan?

737
01:24:14,444 --> 01:24:17,424
This is why I called you.

738
01:24:18,468 --> 01:24:21,318
We will establish a bazaar in İnegöl.

739
01:24:27,516 --> 01:24:31,376
Many caravans will come from Konya and
Constantine...

740
01:24:31,388 --> 01:24:34,648
...and buy your goods.

741
01:24:37,630 --> 01:24:41,920
This trade will bring firstly abundance,
secondly peace...

742
01:24:41,920 --> 01:24:44,546
...to our lands.

743
01:24:44,546 --> 01:24:47,066
Thank you, Majesty.

744
01:24:47,377 --> 01:24:49,546
We are pleased since you came.

745
01:24:49,546 --> 01:24:53,119
Thanks to your presence, we can eat
and feed.

746
01:24:53,119 --> 01:24:54,755
May you always be.

747
01:24:54,755 --> 01:24:56,985
Amen! Amen!
Amen! Amen!

748
01:24:57,051 --> 01:24:58,861
Not at all!

749
01:24:58,861 --> 01:25:02,771
It is Allah who gives sustenance.
We are just a means.

750
01:25:03,886 --> 01:25:07,376
I hope to get the best of everything
for us...

751
01:25:08,612 --> 01:25:11,382
...and for the Lords.

752
01:25:15,342 --> 01:25:17,852
If the vizier Alemşah is the guarantor...

753
01:25:19,607 --> 01:25:22,397
...we will take goods everywhere.

754
01:25:24,112 --> 01:25:26,062
Gündüz Bey.

755
01:25:26,418 --> 01:25:32,288
It is an honor for us to vouch for
a moral trader like you.

756
01:25:33,902 --> 01:25:38,732
The traders who will work with you
are very lucky.

757
01:25:45,562 --> 01:25:48,872
We will be incredibly strong together.

758
01:25:49,134 --> 01:25:51,164
Amen!
Amen!

759
01:25:51,583 --> 01:25:53,903
-Amen.
-I hope so.

760
01:26:05,498 --> 01:26:07,398
Gündüz Bey can have my place...

761
01:26:08,659 --> 01:26:10,409
...if he wants to.

762
01:26:11,928 --> 01:26:14,248
The sky will be a tent for me...

763
01:26:15,541 --> 01:26:17,781
...the sun will be my fire...

764
01:26:19,756 --> 01:26:21,856
...the ground will be my throne.

765
01:26:24,834 --> 01:26:26,924
Wherever I am...

766
01:26:29,581 --> 01:26:31,731
...is the state.

767
01:26:39,028 --> 01:26:41,108
They martyred...

768
01:26:42,217 --> 01:26:44,157
...Prophet Hüseyin.

769
01:26:46,551 --> 01:26:48,161
For what?

770
01:26:49,211 --> 01:26:51,031
For the throne!

771
01:26:53,624 --> 01:26:56,014
Cain killed Abel.

772
01:26:56,583 --> 01:26:58,423
For what?

773
01:26:58,667 --> 01:27:00,557
Because of his ambition.

774
01:27:00,969 --> 01:27:03,119
His jealousy.

775
01:27:06,035 --> 01:27:08,355
Seljuk on one hand...

776
01:27:09,017 --> 01:27:11,157
...Mogul on the other hand.

777
01:27:13,169 --> 01:27:15,449
They are all listening to their demons.

778
01:27:17,000 --> 01:27:18,450
All of them.

779
01:27:19,420 --> 01:27:20,970
However...

780
01:27:24,515 --> 01:27:26,135
...however, I...

781
01:27:26,395 --> 01:27:28,465
...I pray Allah to not make me...

782
01:27:29,266 --> 01:27:30,906
...a prisoner to my demons.

783
01:27:32,526 --> 01:27:34,346
In the name of Allah!

784
01:27:37,704 --> 01:27:40,664
My cause is not the title.

785
01:27:41,942 --> 01:27:45,012
My cause is my love.

786
01:27:46,005 --> 01:27:48,015
It is the red apple.

787
01:27:48,984 --> 01:27:51,474
It is Allah's words.

788
01:27:52,175 --> 01:27:56,755
It is spreading the word to
the whole world.

789
01:27:57,525 --> 01:27:59,745
How great of you!

790
01:28:00,817 --> 01:28:02,737
The lovers don't die!

791
01:28:02,966 --> 01:28:05,016
The lovers don't die!

792
01:28:12,366 --> 01:28:14,456
If my brother is...

793
01:28:16,563 --> 01:28:18,983
...more qualified...

794
01:28:20,366 --> 01:28:22,956
...to carry out my cause...

795
01:28:24,121 --> 01:28:26,391
...then he can.

796
01:28:28,813 --> 01:28:30,613
But...

797
01:28:32,955 --> 01:28:35,545
...if he breaks the cause...

798
01:28:36,564 --> 01:28:38,684
...and succumbs to himself...

799
01:28:42,207 --> 01:28:44,597
...if he tries to stab me in the back...

800
01:28:47,166 --> 01:28:49,966
...like Cain did to Abel...

801
01:28:52,185 --> 01:28:54,045
...then...

802
01:29:00,229 --> 01:29:02,699
...then I won't care he is my brother.

803
01:29:05,839 --> 01:29:07,749
And do what is necessary.

804
01:29:14,345 --> 01:29:15,905
Osman Bey...

805
01:29:16,476 --> 01:29:18,896
...I thought about this but didn't say it.

806
01:29:20,437 --> 01:29:23,977
Obviously, who gave Mari to Nikola is
Gündüz.

807
01:29:28,739 --> 01:29:31,689
I can't let this go without doing
anything.

808
01:29:35,670 --> 01:29:38,700
I told you I'll do what is necessary,
Turgut Bey.

809
01:29:42,854 --> 01:29:46,194
I've never left any cruelty,
any injustice...

810
01:29:47,101 --> 01:29:49,571
...without punishment.

811
01:29:55,110 --> 01:29:57,230
I even beheaded my uncle...

812
01:29:59,993 --> 01:30:02,303
...to ensure justice.

813
01:30:07,873 --> 01:30:12,423
For justice, I won't hesitate to behead...

814
01:30:14,269 --> 01:30:16,759
...even my brother.

815
01:30:18,767 --> 01:30:20,367
Thank you.

816
01:30:23,902 --> 01:30:27,032
My Bey, I have some more news.

817
01:30:29,022 --> 01:30:30,602
The alps.

818
01:30:32,112 --> 01:30:34,952
My Bey, the alps.

819
01:30:37,840 --> 01:30:42,810
They are taking the alps to Konya for
hearing tomorrow.

820
01:30:52,672 --> 01:30:54,352
In that case...

821
01:30:54,847 --> 01:30:57,027
...we will save the alps first.

822
01:30:59,522 --> 01:31:01,812
Tomorrow is the most suitable time...

823
01:31:01,892 --> 01:31:03,662
...to go to Konya.

824
01:31:03,755 --> 01:31:05,655
No.

825
01:31:06,355 --> 01:31:08,705
We will go to Söğüt first.

826
01:31:10,784 --> 01:31:13,454
We will take our alps while
the Vizier is there.

827
01:31:14,417 --> 01:31:16,667
We will destroy...

828
01:31:17,354 --> 01:31:19,334
..that Vizier's reputation.

829
01:31:24,102 --> 01:31:26,092
Now, listen to me carefully.

830
01:31:26,640 --> 01:31:28,550
-Slowly, my Bey.
-Slowly!

831
01:31:30,300 --> 01:31:32,090
Malhun...

832
01:31:32,283 --> 01:31:33,813
...you go to my Sheik.

833
01:31:33,903 --> 01:31:36,473
Tell them to do the belt ceremony for
then Ahis.

834
01:31:38,251 --> 01:31:41,101
Call that snake Vizier too.

835
01:31:41,721 --> 01:31:45,291
Call him so that he gets distracted.

836
01:31:48,039 --> 01:31:50,659
He will think all the Söğüt is obeying
him.

837
01:31:51,300 --> 01:31:55,220
In the meantime, we will save our alps.

838
01:31:56,781 --> 01:31:58,551
As you order, my Bey.

839
01:31:59,218 --> 01:32:00,928
Aygül.

840
01:32:01,194 --> 01:32:05,974
Go to the tribe, talk to Bala.
Keep an eye on...

841
01:32:06,402 --> 01:32:08,482
...my brother and Ayşe Hatun.

842
01:32:08,693 --> 01:32:10,943
I want to know what is going on
in the tribe.

843
01:32:11,014 --> 01:32:12,534
As you order, my Bey.

844
01:32:13,153 --> 01:32:15,473
-Baysungur!
-Yes, my Bey?

845
01:32:15,496 --> 01:32:17,236
Get the horses ready.

846
01:32:17,494 --> 01:32:19,264
As you order, my Bey.

847
01:32:19,663 --> 01:32:23,583
Kumral Abdal, you will inform Kosses.

848
01:32:25,195 --> 01:32:27,075
His sister is with us.

849
01:32:28,415 --> 01:32:30,775
She is safe, he doesn't need to worry.

850
01:32:32,424 --> 01:32:34,854
After what Nikola did to Mari...

851
01:32:35,047 --> 01:32:37,157
...he will want revenge.

852
01:32:38,084 --> 01:32:39,674
As you order, my Bey.

853
01:32:41,246 --> 01:32:43,226
As our enemy is the same...

854
01:32:44,466 --> 01:32:47,036
...Kosses will want to fight with us.

855
01:32:52,114 --> 01:32:56,954
If the safety of the roads is ensured and
where the market will be is finalized...

856
01:32:57,839 --> 01:33:02,079
...everyone will get stronger and richer.

857
01:33:04,498 --> 01:33:08,078
As I understood, Vizier Alemşah...

858
01:33:09,193 --> 01:33:11,693
...our friend Nikola...

859
01:33:12,226 --> 01:33:14,706
...will have more power than us...

860
01:33:15,307 --> 01:33:17,757
...and will get richer than us.

861
01:33:20,044 --> 01:33:23,184
For sure, Kosses. For sure.

862
01:33:24,161 --> 01:33:27,411
Say what you want to say, Lords.

863
01:33:29,111 --> 01:33:31,981
Why not Harmankaya...

864
01:33:32,780 --> 01:33:35,380
...or Bilecik?

865
01:33:35,590 --> 01:33:38,050
Why only İnegöl?

866
01:33:38,437 --> 01:33:40,857
Not only İnegöl.

867
01:33:41,082 --> 01:33:44,222
One month in Söğüt, one month in İnegöl.

868
01:33:45,371 --> 01:33:49,991
If Nikola is ready to make sacrifices...

869
01:33:52,720 --> 01:33:56,330
...we can establish them also
in Harmankaya or Bilecik.

870
01:33:57,790 --> 01:34:01,381
No need for more talking.

871
01:34:01,381 --> 01:34:03,381
It is time for action.

872
01:34:03,888 --> 01:34:06,238
Everyone knows their duty.

873
01:34:07,399 --> 01:34:09,919
Let's get to work.

874
01:34:40,524 --> 01:34:44,764
The Lords freaked out when they heard...

875
01:34:45,374 --> 01:34:47,764
...that the bazaar will be in İnegöl.

876
01:34:50,294 --> 01:34:53,784
But there will be only one, Gündüz Bey.

877
01:34:56,200 --> 01:34:59,290
It is about time they attack each other.

878
01:35:03,752 --> 01:35:06,582
Winning is this easy.

879
01:35:07,829 --> 01:35:12,529
We will shatter the infidels
from the inside...

880
01:35:13,423 --> 01:35:15,783
...without even touching our sword.

881
01:35:18,422 --> 01:35:20,732
Moguls are waiting to attack.

882
01:35:21,425 --> 01:35:24,915
First, we must deal with these.

883
01:35:25,308 --> 01:35:31,298
Then, we will be altogether against
the enemy.

884
01:35:32,275 --> 01:35:33,815
I hope so.

885
01:35:36,829 --> 01:35:38,349
My Bey.

886
01:35:41,169 --> 01:35:43,389
Have you asked the actual question?

887
01:35:49,874 --> 01:35:52,504
What will happen to the mines?

888
01:35:59,348 --> 01:36:02,438
You are right, Master Davut.

889
01:36:08,002 --> 01:36:11,222
They say Kayı's mine now belongs to
the Seljuks.

890
01:36:12,499 --> 01:36:17,269
That mine is the result of the chaos
that Osman created.

891
01:36:20,217 --> 01:36:22,287
We didn't give it to Nikola.

892
01:36:22,782 --> 01:36:24,962
Be happy about this.

893
01:36:27,918 --> 01:36:30,698
It now belongs to the Seljuks...

894
01:36:31,445 --> 01:36:33,935
...to keep the order.

895
01:36:43,221 --> 01:36:44,791
Alright.

896
01:36:45,240 --> 01:36:47,360
Then, excuse us.

897
01:37:22,608 --> 01:37:25,658
We couldn't find Osman, my Vizier.

898
01:37:28,623 --> 01:37:31,773
But I sent soldiers all over the woods.

899
01:37:32,160 --> 01:37:34,250
He has nowhere to go.

900
01:37:36,294 --> 01:37:38,414
I will find him, my Vizier.

901
01:37:39,445 --> 01:37:42,485
If you couldn't find him until now,
Konur...

902
01:37:44,331 --> 01:37:47,881
...obviously, he will come to us.

903
01:37:53,028 --> 01:37:55,718
His alps, Konur.

904
01:37:58,928 --> 01:38:03,118
He will get ready to take them back.

905
01:38:06,181 --> 01:38:08,541
We will be on full alert.

906
01:38:10,709 --> 01:38:14,519
If he does as I say and comes...

907
01:38:15,770 --> 01:38:18,190
...we will catch him.

908
01:38:18,602 --> 01:38:20,902
Then, I will prepare for this, my Vizier.

909
01:38:21,187 --> 01:38:23,547
When we deliver peace and prosperity...

910
01:38:23,927 --> 01:38:27,577
...thanks to this bazaar...

911
01:38:27,822 --> 01:38:29,092
...it won't take long...

912
01:38:30,847 --> 01:38:34,164
...for people to forget about Osman...

913
01:38:34,164 --> 01:38:36,904
...whose reputation is destroyed.

914
01:38:39,997 --> 01:38:42,407
After I get the people's support...

915
01:38:43,536 --> 01:38:44,976
...not the tribe...

916
01:38:45,520 --> 01:38:47,030
...not the Söğüt...

917
01:38:48,180 --> 01:38:50,130
...not the borders...

918
01:38:50,877 --> 01:38:56,677
...but I will be the ruler of all
the Seljuk lands.

919
01:39:00,477 --> 01:39:02,407
What about the Lords...

920
01:39:02,664 --> 01:39:04,704
...Sir?

921
01:39:04,894 --> 01:39:06,304
The Lords?

922
01:39:07,981 --> 01:39:12,711
They are only pawns on this road.

923
01:39:13,446 --> 01:39:15,836
Just like the Turkmens.

924
01:39:19,459 --> 01:39:23,429
I will step on them when I want to.

925
01:39:26,532 --> 01:39:30,952
Now, I am letting them win.

926
01:39:48,371 --> 01:39:49,991
Bala, girl!

927
01:39:50,477 --> 01:39:54,527
Stop drawing circles. My head is
getting dizzy. Sit and wait, please.

928
01:39:58,888 --> 01:40:01,008
There is still no news, mother.

929
01:40:01,648 --> 01:40:03,568
What if they couldn't find Osman?

930
01:40:06,503 --> 01:40:08,479
Look at us!

931
01:40:08,479 --> 01:40:10,339
Ah, my girl, ah!

932
01:40:12,556 --> 01:40:14,126
Are you fine?

933
01:40:14,591 --> 01:40:16,471
I am, mother. I am fine.

934
01:40:16,598 --> 01:40:18,848
It is moving as if it understands.

935
01:40:19,287 --> 01:40:20,997
Oh, my dear.

936
01:40:24,417 --> 01:40:26,367
Can I come in?

937
01:40:27,723 --> 01:40:29,363
Come in, Aygül!

938
01:40:34,969 --> 01:40:37,259
We found Osman Bey, thankfully.

939
01:40:37,392 --> 01:40:38,482
He is well.

940
01:40:38,522 --> 01:40:41,072
Thankfully! Thankfully!

941
01:40:41,072 --> 01:40:43,062
Thankfully!

942
01:40:43,836 --> 01:40:46,036
Thank you, my Allah!

943
01:40:46,530 --> 01:40:48,440
Where is he now?

944
01:40:49,434 --> 01:40:52,164
He is really fine, right?

945
01:40:52,505 --> 01:40:54,615
He is.

946
01:40:55,481 --> 01:40:57,171
Turgut Bey and Mari is with him.

947
01:40:57,171 --> 01:41:00,411
Turgut Bey took Mari back from Nikola.

948
01:41:01,672 --> 01:41:03,452
Thankfully!

949
01:41:05,886 --> 01:41:07,896
Now, listen to me carefully.

950
01:41:09,119 --> 01:41:12,609
Osman Bey believes Gündüz Bey and
Ayşe Hatun...

951
01:41:12,609 --> 01:41:15,899
...are involved in Mari's kidnapping.

952
01:41:17,737 --> 01:41:19,347
What are you saying, Aygül?

953
01:41:19,363 --> 01:41:21,173
How?

954
01:41:22,188 --> 01:41:25,748
Do you remember the sherbet Ayşe Hatun
brought to Mari that night?

955
01:41:28,474 --> 01:41:29,914
So?

956
01:41:30,465 --> 01:41:32,485
Mari fainted after drinking.

957
01:41:33,760 --> 01:41:38,370
The Vizier's soldiers took Mari to Nikola.

958
01:41:39,972 --> 01:41:42,122
How could he?

959
01:41:43,475 --> 01:41:45,551
Ah, Gündüz!

960
01:41:45,551 --> 01:41:49,331
Couldn't we teach you anything?

961
01:41:49,636 --> 01:41:53,526
How could you deliver our guest
to the enemy!

962
01:41:54,910 --> 01:41:56,600
Ayşe Hatun!

963
01:41:57,040 --> 01:41:59,600
She fooled us!

964
01:42:00,601 --> 01:42:03,461
How could she, mother?
This is betrayal!

965
01:42:05,362 --> 01:42:10,032
Osman Bey told us to keep an eye on Ayşe
Hatun and Gündüz Bey...

966
01:42:10,347 --> 01:42:12,927
...but don't get them suspicios.

967
01:42:14,650 --> 01:42:17,480
They will never know we saw Osman Bey.

968
01:42:19,946 --> 01:42:21,850
No secret can be revealed.

969
01:42:21,850 --> 01:42:23,830
Don't worry, my dear.

970
01:42:30,836 --> 01:42:33,906
My Sheik, we will turn the tribe
upside down.

971
01:42:34,279 --> 01:42:36,650
Osman Bey wants us to make
the belt ceremony...

972
01:42:36,650 --> 01:42:38,770
...and gather the people.

973
01:42:39,091 --> 01:42:42,751
He wants you to invite the Vizier too and
show him that you are his subject.

974
01:42:48,110 --> 01:42:50,530
This is a war.

975
01:42:50,728 --> 01:42:55,188
War is not just about weapons.

976
01:42:56,500 --> 01:42:58,830
We will do what Osman Bey says, my girl.

977
01:42:59,861 --> 01:43:02,841
Now, our weapon is our mind.

978
01:43:04,389 --> 01:43:08,199
It is acceptable.

979
01:43:08,915 --> 01:43:10,635
Thank you, my Sheik.

980
01:43:13,559 --> 01:43:15,219
Now...

981
01:43:16,051 --> 01:43:18,781
...let's invite the Vizier first.

982
01:43:22,762 --> 01:43:25,612
Harmankaya Castle

983
01:43:44,245 --> 01:43:46,215
I recognized you.

984
01:43:48,201 --> 01:43:50,411
The madmen in the woods.

985
01:43:51,936 --> 01:43:53,596
Madmen, huh?

986
01:43:53,875 --> 01:43:56,885
Thankfully, I am.

987
01:43:57,080 --> 01:43:59,100
I hope, I am.

988
01:43:59,563 --> 01:44:01,803
You are Osman's madmen.

989
01:44:02,525 --> 01:44:04,405
Rigth?

990
01:44:06,931 --> 01:44:08,771
How dare you?

991
01:44:10,685 --> 01:44:13,415
What kind of bravery is this?

992
01:44:15,012 --> 01:44:19,072
You come to my castle alone.

993
01:44:21,064 --> 01:44:23,634
Do you trust your Allah like the others?

994
01:44:24,299 --> 01:44:27,154
To those who know how to look
can know everything.

995
01:44:27,154 --> 01:44:30,464
Those who don't,
can't see what is in the open.

996
01:44:33,119 --> 01:44:35,659
You can't see Allah by looking up.

997
01:44:35,853 --> 01:44:37,853
You look at your heart to see.

998
01:44:39,822 --> 01:44:43,062
You are too blind, Kosses.

999
01:44:43,086 --> 01:44:45,036
You can't see even if you look.

1000
01:44:45,347 --> 01:44:47,507
But your blindness isn't permanent.

1001
01:44:47,873 --> 01:44:49,451
It will go away one day.

1002
01:44:49,451 --> 01:44:51,391
What are you telling, madmen?

1003
01:44:51,528 --> 01:44:53,678
Cut it short.

1004
01:44:53,843 --> 01:44:57,963
I came so you don't worry about
your sister Mari.

1005
01:45:01,895 --> 01:45:03,685
Her wound is getting better.

1006
01:45:06,819 --> 01:45:08,429
What are you saying?

1007
01:45:10,231 --> 01:45:12,501
What are you talking about?

1008
01:45:13,078 --> 01:45:14,958
Mari is with Nikola.

1009
01:45:15,297 --> 01:45:18,427
No, Mari is not with her executioner.

1010
01:45:18,808 --> 01:45:21,368
Nikola tried to kill her but...

1011
01:45:21,368 --> 01:45:24,128
...Turgut Bey... What a valiant!

1012
01:45:24,541 --> 01:45:27,041
He saved your sister!

1013
01:45:27,966 --> 01:45:30,026
Now, she is with Osman Bey.

1014
01:45:33,170 --> 01:45:34,650
You!

1015
01:45:35,715 --> 01:45:39,925
What are you talking about?

1016
01:45:41,141 --> 01:45:43,881
I thought you were a smart man.

1017
01:45:45,289 --> 01:45:48,329
Did you believe that Nikola demon's word?

1018
01:45:59,416 --> 01:46:01,026
Nikola!

1019
01:46:01,390 --> 01:46:04,890
How long would you keep it a secret?

1020
01:46:08,142 --> 01:46:10,582
Taking revenge from Mari, huh?

1021
01:46:10,915 --> 01:46:14,585
Daring to kill my sister!

1022
01:46:21,344 --> 01:46:23,694
You will pay for this!

1023
01:46:25,123 --> 01:46:26,945
You will!

1024
01:46:26,945 --> 01:46:29,745
-Soldiers! Get ready!
-Stop.

1025
01:46:30,424 --> 01:46:32,184
Take a breath.

1026
01:46:32,379 --> 01:46:34,549
Osman Bey is waiting for you.

1027
01:46:35,283 --> 01:46:40,063
He said ''Kosses is a smart man.
He will see me before Nikola.''.

1028
01:46:40,213 --> 01:46:42,743
He is waiting for you.

1029
01:46:46,229 --> 01:46:49,249
Your secret will be revealed too, Kosses.

1030
01:47:03,406 --> 01:47:06,496
Turkish tribes will prosper, I hope.

1031
01:47:06,940 --> 01:47:12,030
We made a deal with our old friends,
the Lords and Vizier Alemşah.

1032
01:47:15,370 --> 01:47:18,850
A grand bazaar will be established
in İnegöl.

1033
01:47:20,470 --> 01:47:23,080
There is no such thing as an old friend.

1034
01:47:25,128 --> 01:47:28,118
Snake tongued Alemşah is poisoning you.

1035
01:47:28,217 --> 01:47:30,337
Open your eyes already!

1036
01:47:31,755 --> 01:47:34,105
You are talking to the Bey of the tribe,
mother.

1037
01:47:40,022 --> 01:47:42,212
He is the Bey of the tribe, mother.

1038
01:47:45,214 --> 01:47:48,044
I am talking to the Bey of the tribe,
right?

1039
01:47:50,217 --> 01:47:52,147
You are right.

1040
01:47:52,524 --> 01:47:55,244
I talk and talk but...

1041
01:47:58,010 --> 01:48:01,580
...his blind eyes can't see
what's right...

1042
01:48:01,983 --> 01:48:04,093
...or wrong.

1043
01:48:07,232 --> 01:48:09,702
Where is Osman Bey, Gündüz Bey?

1044
01:48:10,537 --> 01:48:12,287
How is he?

1045
01:48:13,206 --> 01:48:17,138
Are you worried for prosperity when you
don't know if your brother is alive?

1046
01:48:17,138 --> 01:48:19,148
Don't cross the line, Bala Hatun!

1047
01:48:25,125 --> 01:48:27,095
I don't want to break your heart.

1048
01:48:28,071 --> 01:48:30,116
But I am the Bey of Kayı!

1049
01:48:30,116 --> 01:48:32,426
We are here to talk about the future of
the Kayı!

1050
01:48:32,464 --> 01:48:34,824
I don't want to hear anything else!

1051
01:48:37,613 --> 01:48:41,443
The deal we made with Vizier Alemşah
will solve...

1052
01:48:41,651 --> 01:48:44,071
...all the problems of our people.

1053
01:48:44,548 --> 01:48:48,678
You still talk about trade, Vizier!

1054
01:48:49,335 --> 01:48:51,559
There is no Bey, no alp.

1055
01:48:51,559 --> 01:48:53,469
Master Davut!

1056
01:48:53,798 --> 01:48:57,348
My respect for your age is about to
run out!

1057
01:49:01,175 --> 01:49:05,095
What I say is for the sake of the whole
Turks.

1058
01:49:06,018 --> 01:49:08,628
We kept and kept fighting.

1059
01:49:08,865 --> 01:49:11,545
Shouldn't this tribe get better?

1060
01:49:12,026 --> 01:49:14,856
Shouldn't these people take a breath?

1061
01:49:19,362 --> 01:49:21,082
Can we come in?

1062
01:49:21,977 --> 01:49:23,687
Patience, patience.

1063
01:49:24,569 --> 01:49:26,359
Come in.

1064
01:49:35,301 --> 01:49:38,331
Sheik Edebalı sent his greetings,
Gündüz Bey.

1065
01:49:39,502 --> 01:49:42,602
There will be the belt ceremony in Söğüt
tomorrow.

1066
01:49:43,955 --> 01:49:46,745
Vizier Alemşah is one of our guests.

1067
01:49:48,856 --> 01:49:51,776
My Sheik expects you too.

1068
01:49:54,407 --> 01:49:56,537
I'd like to come, Akça Dervish.

1069
01:49:57,226 --> 01:50:01,716
But I will visit the new bazaar in İnegöl
tomorrow.

1070
01:50:02,537 --> 01:50:04,377
Next time.

1071
01:50:05,759 --> 01:50:07,679
Send my love to my Sheik.

1072
01:50:27,880 --> 01:50:30,630
I came to ask for permission.

1073
01:50:30,962 --> 01:50:35,662
If you allow, we would like to hold
a belt ceremony...

1074
01:50:35,663 --> 01:50:39,893
...for the journeymen's transition
to mastery tomorrow.

1075
01:50:41,432 --> 01:50:44,959
Of course!
Of course!

1076
01:50:44,959 --> 01:50:49,879
How could we say no to our Sheik Edebalı?

1077
01:50:50,851 --> 01:50:52,441
You can, of course!

1078
01:50:52,441 --> 01:50:54,801
I would like to see you there...

1079
01:50:56,022 --> 01:50:59,932
...while our children get their mastery...

1080
01:51:00,503 --> 01:51:02,483
...Vizier Alemşah.

1081
01:51:03,005 --> 01:51:05,985
I am actually deeply honored.

1082
01:51:06,069 --> 01:51:07,839
And surprised.

1083
01:51:07,947 --> 01:51:12,837
Don't be. Now, me and all the other Ahis
are your subjects.

1084
01:51:13,517 --> 01:51:15,844
We want the whole Söğüt to see this.

1085
01:51:15,844 --> 01:51:17,574
Good!

1086
01:51:17,841 --> 01:51:20,191
Good, Sheik Edebalı!

1087
01:51:20,419 --> 01:51:22,789
I would love to be there.

1088
01:51:23,976 --> 01:51:25,685
Thank you.

1089
01:51:25,685 --> 01:51:28,095
If you'll excuse me.

1090
01:51:32,494 --> 01:51:34,654
There is a lot of work to do.

1091
01:51:34,870 --> 01:51:36,540
Of course, here you go.

1092
01:51:37,710 --> 01:51:39,070
Thank you.

1093
01:51:52,052 --> 01:51:55,332
Edebalı is a very dangerous man, Konur.

1094
01:51:56,152 --> 01:51:59,702
It is obvious he is in contact with Osman.

1095
01:52:00,790 --> 01:52:03,020
They are playing a game.

1096
01:52:05,224 --> 01:52:09,134
I will let them play their game.

1097
01:52:09,953 --> 01:52:11,763
For now.

1098
01:52:13,482 --> 01:52:16,422
Tomorrow, while I am with Ahis...

1099
01:52:16,954 --> 01:52:18,954
...look sharp.

1100
01:52:27,089 --> 01:52:30,199
My Bey, I heard from the blacksmith.

1101
01:52:30,882 --> 01:52:33,272
Vizier is establishing a bazaar in İnegöl.

1102
01:52:38,759 --> 01:52:41,379
That vile Vizier's goal is to...

1103
01:52:42,892 --> 01:52:45,862
...get the Lords richer and...

1104
01:52:46,946 --> 01:52:49,146
...earn reputation.

1105
01:52:51,764 --> 01:52:54,344
It is against everything I do.

1106
01:52:55,388 --> 01:52:59,908
He is promising fake peace to people.

1107
01:53:01,522 --> 01:53:03,140
Can I come in?

1108
01:53:03,140 --> 01:53:04,790
Come in!

1109
01:53:08,003 --> 01:53:09,753
My Bey.

1110
01:53:14,118 --> 01:53:15,628
Come in.

1111
01:53:18,326 --> 01:53:19,886
Mari!

1112
01:53:23,336 --> 01:53:25,016
My sister!
Are you fine?

1113
01:53:27,649 --> 01:53:31,849
Mari, whom you left to Nikola and tried
to kill.

1114
01:53:37,911 --> 01:53:40,581
Did you just remember I am your sister?

1115
01:53:41,895 --> 01:53:43,295
Mari, I just--

1116
01:53:43,363 --> 01:53:46,603
Don't, Kosses!
Stay back.

1117
01:53:49,843 --> 01:53:51,283
Stop.

1118
01:53:57,769 --> 01:54:00,789
I just wanted you to have a good life.

1119
01:54:01,659 --> 01:54:05,329
I won't let that bastard Nikola get away
with what he has done.

1120
01:54:07,220 --> 01:54:11,010
I promise you, I will hurt him such that
...

1121
01:54:26,329 --> 01:54:28,629
Now we have a common enemy.

1122
01:54:31,556 --> 01:54:33,596
Whatever it takes.

1123
01:54:35,932 --> 01:54:37,652
Osman Bey.

1124
01:54:38,252 --> 01:54:42,872
I am ready to unite with you
to make their life a living hell.

1125
01:54:49,137 --> 01:54:53,297
There will be a belt ceremony in Söğüt.

1126
01:54:54,526 --> 01:54:56,816
If you are that sincere...

1127
01:54:57,115 --> 01:54:59,575
...you will get us into Söğüt.

1128
01:55:03,713 --> 01:55:05,183
Alright.

1129
01:55:06,774 --> 01:55:09,514
You will get into Söğüt without
any suspect.

1130
01:55:11,402 --> 01:55:14,002
Samuel will get you inside.

1131
01:55:19,269 --> 01:55:21,699
If you lose us...

1132
01:55:22,798 --> 01:55:25,418
...there will be no one left in these
lands.

1133
01:55:26,996 --> 01:55:29,306
Being alone means...

1134
01:55:30,249 --> 01:55:34,599
...being a prey.

1135
01:55:36,881 --> 01:55:41,791
I am neither a hunter nor a prey,
Osman Bey.

1136
01:55:43,011 --> 01:55:46,761
I am just a wounded man who has
been betrayed by his closest ones...

1137
01:55:47,641 --> 01:55:52,531
... and wants to avenge his sister.

1138
01:55:53,411 --> 01:55:55,391
You can trust me.

1139
01:56:23,974 --> 01:56:25,344
Stop!

1140
01:56:28,470 --> 01:56:29,550
Why are you here?

1141
01:56:29,726 --> 01:56:32,756
I brought the presents of Lord Kossess
for Vizier Alam Shah.

1142
01:57:23,822 --> 01:57:25,932
Let them pass!

1143
01:57:58,451 --> 01:58:01,491
- Salam Aleikum.
- Alaikum Salam.

1144
01:58:04,226 --> 01:58:07,166
Seljuq's valiant soldiers!

1145
01:58:07,995 --> 01:58:10,785
All the Sogut drank this sherbet!

1146
01:58:10,785 --> 01:58:13,595
I wanted to offer you too.

1147
01:58:16,145 --> 01:58:17,795
Thank you.

1148
01:58:35,888 --> 01:58:37,538
May Allah bless you.

1149
01:58:37,804 --> 01:58:39,804
May it heal you.

1150
01:58:45,405 --> 01:58:50,375
I seek refuge in Allah
from the accursed satan.

1151
01:58:52,124 --> 01:58:57,784
In the name of Allah, the most merciful,
the most compassionate.

1152
01:58:59,563 --> 01:59:05,043
"And do not crave what
Allah has given some of you over others...

1153
01:59:05,043 --> 01:59:11,989
...Men will be rewarded
according to their deeds...

1154
01:59:12,009 --> 01:59:19,059
...and women ˹equally˺
according to theirs...

1155
01:59:19,171 --> 01:59:27,951
...Rather, ask Allah for His bounties...

1156
01:59:28,431 --> 01:59:44,714
...Surely Allah has ˹perfect˺
knowledge of all things.
[Surah An-Nisa - 1-176]

1157
01:59:45,214 --> 01:59:50,984
Allah Almighty speaks the truth.

1158
01:59:56,112 --> 01:59:58,102
Respect!

1159
02:00:16,257 --> 02:00:19,037
As-Salam Aleikum people of sharia.

1160
02:00:22,249 --> 02:00:25,149
As-Salam Aleikum people of Tariqa

1161
02:00:28,972 --> 02:00:31,902
As- Salam Aleikum

1162
02:00:34,264 --> 02:00:37,494
As-Salam Aleikum people of truth.

1163
02:00:44,963 --> 02:00:46,943
Tell me, the head of valiants.

1164
02:00:48,491 --> 02:00:50,261
What is the occupation of...

1165
02:00:51,572 --> 02:00:53,702
...the apprentice boy...

1166
02:00:54,136 --> 02:00:56,026
...that you want Ijazah?

1167
02:00:57,585 --> 02:01:02,255
He seeks your prayers under the sky...

1168
02:01:02,973 --> 02:01:07,103
He seeks your prayers on the grass...

1169
02:01:07,114 --> 02:01:11,854
The leatherman apprentice Ahmet.

1170
02:01:13,560 --> 02:01:15,460
He wanted to.

1171
02:01:17,154 --> 02:01:19,564
...came into your presence.

1172
02:01:42,748 --> 02:01:44,558
Not much left.

1173
02:01:48,337 --> 02:01:50,607
Your suffering will end.

1174
02:01:53,767 --> 02:01:55,677
You are going to Konya.

1175
02:01:58,910 --> 02:02:01,790
We'll send your Osman Bey after you.

1176
02:02:02,599 --> 02:02:03,939
Either alive...

1177
02:02:05,480 --> 02:02:06,710
...or dead.

1178
02:02:10,794 --> 02:02:16,404
Do not speak of my Bey with your
stinky mouth!

1179
02:02:16,984 --> 02:02:18,972
You'll see now!

1180
02:02:28,119 --> 02:02:29,989
Coward!

1181
02:02:30,091 --> 02:02:32,341
Untie us!

1182
02:02:32,380 --> 02:02:34,260
Ignoble dog!

1183
02:02:41,213 --> 02:02:43,015
Ignoble!

1184
02:02:43,015 --> 02:02:44,925
Untie us!

1185
02:02:52,804 --> 02:02:54,544
Brother!

1186
02:02:54,890 --> 02:02:56,560
Are you okay?

1187
02:03:05,597 --> 02:03:07,557
Keep your eyes open!

1188
02:03:08,059 --> 02:03:10,409
Do not let anyone near!

1189
02:03:16,528 --> 02:03:19,198
Did you think I would forget you?

1190
02:03:19,221 --> 02:03:22,151
Would I ever forget you?
I am always here.

1191
02:03:22,449 --> 02:03:24,449
Drink it.

1192
02:03:27,778 --> 02:03:29,388
This is Ahi Sherbet.

1193
02:03:29,418 --> 02:03:32,528
I want all of you to drink it.

1194
02:03:33,403 --> 02:03:35,263
May Allah bless you.

1195
02:03:35,335 --> 02:03:38,125
Thank you very much.

1196
02:03:39,931 --> 02:03:42,181
May it heal you, my valiants.

1197
02:03:50,290 --> 02:03:52,768
I want to offer to the vailants inside.

1198
02:03:52,768 --> 02:03:55,478
No.
There are captives inside.

1199
02:04:45,097 --> 02:04:47,637
Now it is time to get the Alps.

1200
02:04:49,181 --> 02:04:50,851
Let's go.

1201
02:04:53,685 --> 02:04:57,155
Kumral Abdal, bring Alps clothes.

1202
02:04:58,113 --> 02:04:59,963
Yes my Bey.

1203
02:05:09,866 --> 02:05:11,576
Come on.

1204
02:05:51,661 --> 02:05:53,701
Have this pocket.

1205
02:05:55,328 --> 02:05:58,848
Alps are going to Konya.
Get lost for a while.

1206
02:05:59,538 --> 02:06:01,818
It's Vizier Alam Shah's order!

1207
02:06:04,980 --> 02:06:06,940
Betrayer!
Betrayer!

1208
02:06:07,052 --> 02:06:09,752
Betrayer dog!

1209
02:06:11,144 --> 02:06:13,634
Betrayers don't live long, Bahadir!

1210
02:06:13,704 --> 02:06:15,683
Betrayers don't live long, Bahadir!

1211
02:06:15,683 --> 02:06:17,143
Eyvallah. (thanks)

1212
02:06:18,658 --> 02:06:22,178
Stop, not this way.
Take the back exit.

1213
02:06:22,851 --> 02:06:24,122
Eyvallah (okay.)

1214
02:06:24,122 --> 02:06:26,872
- Ignoble dog!
- Shame on you!

1215
02:06:36,297 --> 02:06:37,887
Osman Bey!

1216
02:06:39,629 --> 02:06:41,479
Yeah, Osman Bey.

1217
02:06:55,862 --> 02:06:59,092
You ignoble dog!

1218
02:07:02,255 --> 02:07:04,935
You sold your honor for gold!

1219
02:07:10,892 --> 02:07:15,712
You are going to pay for what
happened to my Alps.

1220
02:07:19,037 --> 02:07:21,097
Come here!

1221
02:07:21,099 --> 02:07:22,489
Tell me...

1222
02:07:23,067 --> 02:07:25,257
...are you the betrayer in the tribe?

1223
02:07:25,851 --> 02:07:27,441
Tell me!

1224
02:07:32,996 --> 02:07:34,956
I am not only the betrayer.

1225
02:07:35,288 --> 02:07:37,988
I caused Karayel's death as well.

1226
02:07:58,725 --> 02:08:00,525
Karayel!

1227
02:08:39,968 --> 02:08:41,558
Thank Allah, my Bey.

1228
02:08:43,132 --> 02:08:44,782
Brothers!

1229
02:08:52,990 --> 02:08:54,330
My Bey!

1230
02:08:54,838 --> 02:08:56,368
My Bey!

1231
02:08:56,898 --> 02:08:58,448
My Bey!

1232
02:08:59,230 --> 02:09:00,420
My Bey!

1233
02:09:01,545 --> 02:09:03,575
- My Bey, how is your wound?
- It's okay.

1234
02:09:03,575 --> 02:09:05,827
- Are you fine?
- We are fine, my Bey.

1235
02:09:10,140 --> 02:09:11,670
Let's go.

1236
02:09:32,074 --> 02:09:33,770
Welcome Osman Bey?

1237
02:09:33,770 --> 02:09:37,580
What's that? Are you going to ask us
to drop our weapons again?

1238
02:09:44,180 --> 02:09:45,680
Come here.

1239
02:09:46,155 --> 02:09:47,945
Soldiers!

1240
02:10:35,405 --> 02:10:37,005
Come.

1241
02:10:54,080 --> 02:10:55,970
This is for the spear.

1242
02:11:04,108 --> 02:11:07,888
And this is for all Alps!

1243
02:11:28,462 --> 02:11:30,152
Let's go alps!

1244
02:11:36,743 --> 02:11:38,493
Hey son.

1245
02:11:39,428 --> 02:11:44,938
We bless your body.
May Allah bless your soul.

1246
02:11:46,427 --> 02:11:51,197
Abide by sharia and justification
in trading.

1247
02:11:51,979 --> 02:11:56,929
Watch your hands and tongue.

1248
02:11:57,970 --> 02:12:01,370
Use your scales truthfully.

1249
02:12:04,015 --> 02:12:06,085
Kiss your master's hand.

1250
02:12:17,276 --> 02:12:18,906
Praise be.

1251
02:12:18,975 --> 02:12:20,725
Praise be.

1252
02:12:33,763 --> 02:12:35,653
Hadrat Vizier.

1253
02:12:37,053 --> 02:12:39,963
Osman Bey is here.
He took the Alps.

1254
02:12:44,649 --> 02:12:46,499
Osman!

1255
02:12:51,088 --> 02:12:52,778
Sheik Edebali.

1256
02:12:55,389 --> 02:12:57,869
We appreciate it all.

1257
02:12:58,364 --> 02:13:01,234
But we have an important issue.

1258
02:13:01,413 --> 02:13:03,043
We have to go immediately.

1259
02:13:03,783 --> 02:13:06,493
We are going to see each other
again eventually.

1260
02:13:07,101 --> 02:13:08,761
Eyvallah (sure).

1261
02:13:08,927 --> 02:13:12,319
Your arrival pleased us...

1262
02:13:12,319 --> 02:13:13,779
...Hadrat Vizier.

1263
02:13:15,809 --> 02:13:17,219
Salute for you.

1264
02:13:47,855 --> 02:13:49,595
Where are we going, my Bey?

1265
02:13:53,245 --> 02:13:55,465
Our destination is Inegol!

1266
02:13:57,690 --> 02:13:59,580
Let's go alps!

1267
02:14:04,057 --> 02:14:14,427
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com